---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config.js';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy" description={`How ${SITE.name} collects, uses and protects personal information.`}>
  <section class="page-head"><div class="wrap"><h1>Privacy policy</h1><p>Draft, for the club to review before launch.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p>{SITE.name} ("the club") follows British Columbia's <em>Personal Information Protection Act</em> (PIPA).</p>
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>When you register, we collect the student's name and date of birth, a parent or guardian's name for students under 18, contact details, emergency contact, optional medical notes, previous experience, and how you heard about us.</p>
      <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To register students and contact families about classes</li>
        <li>To keep students safe in class and reach someone in an emergency</li>
        <li>To manage club membership and ISKF gradings</li>
        <li>To understand how people find the club (the "how did you hear" question)</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Who sees it</h2>
      <p>Only club instructors and administrators. We do not sell or share your information, except with the ISKF where needed for membership and gradings, or where the law requires it.</p>
      <h2>How we protect it</h2>
      <p>Registrations are stored in a secure database. The admin area requires an individual login for each authorised club member. Medical information is used only for safety in class.</p>
      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>For as long as the student is a member, and up to two years afterwards, unless you ask us to delete it sooner.</p>
      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You can ask to see, correct or delete your information at any time. Contact our privacy contact at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
      <h2>Photos</h2>
      <p>We only use photos of students on our website and social media when consent was given on the registration form. You can withdraw consent at any time.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
